.TH LUS-AST 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-ast \- print the syntax tree of a file as JSON
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus ast\fR [\-\-no\-comments] [\-\-no\-recover] file
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the syntax tree of a file as JSON, for tools that analyze or transform Lus code.
The tree has the same nodes as the result of \fBdebug.parse\fR.
Syntax trees describes the tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-comments\fR
Omit comments from the tree.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-recover\fR
Stop at the first syntax error.
Without it, the parser continues past an error and lists every error in the tree.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The file parsed without errors.
.TP
1
The tree lists syntax errors.
.TP
2
An option is malformed or the file cannot be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-ast, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
